WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.091 --> 00:00:15.431
screamed as the fire consumed his arm.

2
00:00:16.252 --> 00:00:20.073
Hoping to create more friction, he started to rub his other hand against his side.

3
00:00:20.093 --> 00:00:23.934
"Stop!" Wyssa's harsh voice rang out.

4
00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:26.734
A moment later the fire was gone.

5
00:00:27.595 --> 00:00:31.236
Zann felt Wyssa touch his hand and arm, and the pain disappeared.

6
00:00:32.428 --> 00:00:32.868
"What happened?"

7
00:00:33.128 --> 00:00:33.749
Perda asked.

8
00:00:33.769 --> 00:00:35.610
"Why is it so dark here?"

9
00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.311
A cool white flame appeared in Wyssa's hands.

10
00:00:40.252 --> 00:00:45.314
Wyssa dropped it on the ground, and it spread to surround her, Zann, and Perda so they could

11
00:00:45.354 --> 00:00:46.395
see one another clearly.

12
00:00:46.415 --> 00:00:49.917
"You'll need to be careful here," Wyssa said.

13
00:00:50.397 --> 00:00:51.818
Her voice was calm now.

14
00:00:51.838 --> 00:00:56.520
"Galvan is a land of extra-strong magic energy.

15
00:00:57.448 --> 00:01:04.072
Any magic you perform will be greatly intensified, often in unpredictable ways."

16
00:01:05.193 --> 00:01:07.094
Zann could still hear a buzzing sound.

17
00:01:08.235 --> 00:01:11.457
Now he realized it was the steady hum of magic energy.

18
00:01:11.477 --> 00:01:14.559
"Let me try some magic."

19
00:01:15.079 --> 00:01:16.320
Perda sounded intrigued.

20
00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.081
She snapped her fingers.

21
00:01:18.581 --> 00:01:20.743
A cup of airberry juice appeared in her hand.

22
00:01:20.763 --> 00:01:22.504
"There," she said.

23
00:01:22.828 --> 00:01:28.812
"That didn't—" She gasped as the airberry juice expanded and flowed over the edge of the cup like

24
00:01:28.852 --> 00:01:29.392
a fountain.

25
00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:32.174
Soon all three of them were drenched.

26
00:01:33.515 --> 00:01:34.796
"No more magic!"

27
00:01:35.096 --> 00:01:35.796
Wyssa snapped.

28
00:01:36.737 --> 00:01:39.579
She waved her hand, and the airberry juice disappeared.

29
00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.780
"Wow," Perda said.

30
00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:46.023
"Just imagine what someone with Morb's powers could do in a place like this!"

31
00:01:47.123 --> 00:01:48.104
Wyssa glared at her.

32
00:01:48.904 --> 00:01:54.447
Zann wasn't sure if that was because of the airberry juice stunt, or because Perda had mentioned Morb's

33
00:01:54.527 --> 00:02:00.651
name. "Don't do any magic, either of you," Wyssa said sternly.

34
00:02:00.671 --> 00:02:02.472
"Leave it to me."

35
00:02:02.492 --> 00:02:04.793
"Okay," Zann said.

36
00:02:04.813 --> 00:02:08.755
"Now, how are we supposed to figure out whether our friends are here?"

37
00:02:08.775 --> 00:02:12.297
"I'm going to do a Seeking spell," Wyssa said.

38
00:02:12.317 --> 00:02:13.678
"Join hands."

39
00:02:14.678 --> 00:02:18.716
Zann took Perda's hand and then reached for Wyssa's.

40
00:02:18.736 --> 00:02:21.977
Wyssa grabbed his wrist with one hand and snapped her fingers.

41
00:02:23.417 --> 00:02:27.658
A second later all three of them were yanked off their feet and flying through the air.

42
00:02:27.678 --> 00:02:30.239
"Whoa!" Perda yelled.

43
00:02:30.259 --> 00:02:31.580
"What's happening?"

44
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.840
"It's the Seeking spell," Zann called back.

45
00:02:35.561 --> 00:02:38.101
They were moving so fast he couldn't see a thing.

46
00:02:38.121 --> 00:02:43.203
"The intense magic here must be affecting the spell, like Wyssa said.

47
00:02:44.023 --> 00:02:45.663
It's pulling us toward the others!

48
00:02:46.103 --> 00:02:48.144
That means they're definitely here, right?"

49
00:02:49.416 --> 00:02:51.437
"Not necessarily," Wyssa replied.

50
00:02:51.457 --> 00:02:55.439
"A Seeking spell can't be used to find one particular person.

51
00:02:56.219 --> 00:02:58.640
Don't they teach you anything in those Magica schools?"

52
00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:02.281
"We haven't really done Seeking spells yet," Perda said.

53
00:03:02.301 --> 00:03:03.982
"At least not in school."

54
00:03:04.002 --> 00:03:08.384
"Well, we're Seeking anything from Magica," Wyssa explained.

55
00:03:08.404 --> 00:03:12.666
"The spell could be leading us to your friends, or—oh!"

56
00:03:14.326 --> 00:03:18.248
They flew through the doorway of a small cottage and came to a sudden stop.

57
00:03:19.096 --> 00:03:24.759
A short man with large ears and feet was staring at them with a look of total surprise.

58
00:03:24.779 --> 00:03:27.761
"Zann!" Perda pointed toward a table.

59
00:03:27.781 --> 00:03:32.364
"It's your parents' book— Creatures of the Known Magical Worlds!"

60
00:03:33.445 --> 00:03:34.265
Zann gasped.

61
00:03:34.845 --> 00:03:36.086
"What's that doing here?"

62
00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:39.368
Wyssa smiled at the strange little man.

63
00:03:39.388 --> 00:03:42.010
"Greetings, Fud," she said.

64
00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:45.912
"I should have realized where my Seeking spell was leading us."

65
00:03:46.936 --> 00:03:49.357
Fud smiled and clasped her hand.

66
00:03:49.377 --> 00:03:52.619
"Wyssa! What a wonderful surprise!"

67
00:03:53.579 --> 00:03:54.920
Zann was pretty surprised too.

68
00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:01.683
First the Niffians had greeted Wyssa like an old friend, and now Fud was doing the same.

69
00:04:02.603 --> 00:04:07.005
Until now Zann hadn't thought of Wyssa as the type of person who had many friends.

70
00:04:07.505 --> 00:04:09.206
Or any friends, really.

71
00:04:09.226 --> 00:04:11.487
"Where did you get this?"

72
00:04:11.847 --> 00:04:13.788
Zann asked Fud, picking up the book.

73
00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:16.841
"Wyssa brought it to me," Fud replied.

74
00:04:16.861 --> 00:04:19.942
"She knows of my interest in other worlds."

75
00:04:20.843 --> 00:04:23.144
"Have you visited many of the worlds in the book?"

76
00:04:23.564 --> 00:04:24.124
asked Perda.

77
00:04:24.144 --> 00:04:28.886
"Sadly, I've visited none of them," Fud said with a wry smile.

78
00:04:28.906 --> 00:04:33.868
"We Galvanites can barely manage to feed ourselves with our weak magic.

79
00:04:34.708 --> 00:04:37.169
I'd have little chance of surviving the vortex."

80
00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:39.770
"Really?" Zann said.

81
00:04:39.791 --> 00:04:43.132
"But this world has such strong magic energy!"

82
00:04:44.084 --> 00:04:45.845
"That's true," Wyssa said.

83
00:04:45.865 --> 00:04:52.807
"And as you saw "—she glared at Perda—"it can be dangerous to perform magic in such a place.

84
00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:57.068
The Galvanites have evolved to avoid that danger."

85
00:04:57.948 --> 00:05:01.269
She went on to tell Fud about their search for Darb, Gliss, and Zing.

86
00:05:01.289 --> 00:05:03.990
"Oh, dear," Fud said.

87
00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:06.931
"I'll send out a message to see if they've been spotted."

88
00:05:08.111 --> 00:05:10.412
With the others following, he hurried outside.

89
00:05:11.604 --> 00:05:15.267
"If these people don't have much magic, how can he send a message?"

90
00:05:15.607 --> 00:05:16.207
Perda wondered.

91
00:05:16.227 --> 00:05:19.009
"Just watch," Wyssa said.

92
00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:23.392
Fud began stomping his large bare feet on the ground.

93
00:05:24.573 --> 00:05:28.576
The sound echoed like a drumbeat as the constant magic energy caught it.

94
00:05:29.516 --> 00:05:32.978
Soon the rhythm was vibrating all around Zann and the others.

95
00:05:33.859 --> 00:05:35.980
Before long they heard another rhythm.

96
00:05:36.001 --> 00:05:38.522
"Is that someone answering?"

97
00:05:38.862 --> 00:05:39.443
Zann asked.

98
00:05:39.463 --> 00:05:43.862
"Yes." Fud frowned with concentration as he listened.

99
00:05:43.882 --> 00:05:46.603
"And here comes another response."

100
00:05:47.844 --> 00:05:51.566
For the next few minutes, more and more drumbeats came from all directions.

101
00:05:52.506 --> 00:05:54.667
Finally, though, Fud shook his head.

102
00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:59.650
"I'm sorry," he said, "but it seems nobody has seen your friends."

103
00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:05.613
"That means they're likely not in Galvan," Wyssa said with a sigh.

104
00:06:05.633 --> 00:06:09.896
"Especially since my Seeking spell didn't find them either.

105
00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:11.500
Thank you, Fud.

106
00:06:12.001 --> 00:06:13.682
We'd better get back to the wormhole."

107
00:06:14.942 --> 00:06:17.664
"Please visit again soon," Fud urged her.

108
00:06:17.684 --> 00:06:19.565
"I will, my friend."

109
00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:22.046
Wyssa grabbed Zann and Perda.

110
00:06:22.066 --> 00:06:24.808
"Zap!" Splash!

111
00:06:24.828 --> 00:06:30.251
"Drat!" Zann had landed in a muddy stream, and his legs were soaked.

112
00:06:31.031 --> 00:06:33.793
"This doesn't look like the right spot," Perda said.

113
00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:36.935
She and Wyssa had landed on the stream bank.

114
00:06:36.955 --> 00:06:39.036
"Where's the wormhole?"

115
00:06:39.956 --> 00:06:40.657
Wyssa shrugged.

116
00:06:40.677 --> 00:06:44.739
"As I said, magic can be unpredictable here."

117
00:06:45.479 --> 00:06:50.742
Zann climbed out of the stream and rubbed his hands, automatically conjuring dry pants and shoes.

118
00:06:51.943 --> 00:06:56.145
A second later he was wrapped in reams of heavy fabric from head to toe.

119
00:06:56.165 --> 00:06:57.986
"Help!" he gasped.

120
00:06:58.006 --> 00:06:59.627
"I can't breathe!"
